{"id": "striviaqa0138", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The first ever con certo for tuba and orchestra was composed by the American tub a player William Bell. He wrote it in 19 72, which is actually pretty amazing considering how rare concert os are for low brass instruments back then. It helped bring more attention to the tuba as an instrument capable of solo performance s rather than just being part of the rhythm section or support ing role. So yes, William Bell is the composer you're looking for.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
