{"id": "striviaqa0186", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The only U. S. president who didn't speak English as his first language was Gro ver Cleveland. He was born in New York, but his mother was from a Scottish family and spoke with a strong Scottish accent. So while he learned English early on, it wasn't the first language he picked up.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
